<p>I'm&#8230; a little iffy on this. Initially I was strongly leaning for an upvote, but the last addendum&#8230;</p>
<p>The last addendum is basically a lot of technobabble which only says &quot;This is a compulsion effect.&quot; There is no additional meaning in the language you used, just getting that exact same idea across. It's capable of <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">psychically</span> physiologically-ish compelling them to silence and complacency through <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">magic</span> anomalous action at a distance.</p>
<p>Kind of the same idea, telling us the mechanism for a compulsion effect or pointing out that it can be resisted without changing the outcomes doesn't improve anything. (For a discussion of why this is a problem, including how it pertains to this article, see <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-1526851/critiquing-compulsion-addiction-effects#post-2434607">this comment</a> by someone smarter than me.)</p>
<p>I don't think it would even have been such a dig deal if it hadn't been your last-addendum security-locked 'twist.' As it is, it feels like you just used a whole addendum to hang a big banner on the weakest part of your article.</p>
<p>No vote.</p>

